module

public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.FineSaturatedLogBlowup
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Submonoid.Saturation
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.Subgroup.Saturated
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.QuotientGroup.Defs

/-!
# The subgroup generated by a face is saturated

Source: Illusie--Laszlo--Orgogozo, Exposé VIII, §§3.1.1--3.1.2 and Remark 3.1.10(i),
printed pp. 98--99 (blueprint: lem-trf-face-subgroup-saturated).

`AddSaturated` expresses the face condition, whereas `NSMulSaturated` expresses closure
under taking positive integral roots. The group completion is Mathlib's additive version
of the canonical completion used in `FineSaturatedLogBlowup`. No finite generation or
sharpness hypothesis is imposed.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

namespace AddSubmonoid

/-- In an integral saturated commutative monoid, the subgroup generated by a face is
saturated, and the quotient of the group completion by this subgroup is torsion-free.
Source: ILO, Exposé VIII, §§3.1.1--3.1.2 and Remark 3.1.10(i), printed pp. 98--99
(blueprint: lem-trf-face-subgroup-saturated).

Proof (the direct argument recorded in the node): let `n > 0` and `n • g = a - b`
with `a, b` images of elements of the face. Put `h = g + b`. Then
`n • h = a + (n - 1) • b` belongs to the face, hence to the image of the monoid.
Saturation puts `h` in that image. As `n • h = h + (n - 1) • h`, the face condition
puts `h` in the face. Thus `g = h - b` lies in its generated subgroup. Finally an
element of the quotient killed by a positive integer is zero by this root-closure
property, which says precisely that the quotient is torsion-free. -/
theorem face_subgroup_saturated (Q : Type u) [AddCommMonoid Q]
    (h_integral : Function.Injective (Algebra.GrothendieckAddGroup.of (M := Q)))
    (h_saturated :
      (AddMonoidHom.mrange (Algebra.GrothendieckAddGroup.of (M := Q))).NSMulSaturated)
    (F : AddSubmonoid Q) (h_face : F.AddSaturated) :
    (AddSubgroup.closure (Algebra.GrothendieckAddGroup.of '' (F : Set Q))).NSMulSaturated ∧
      IsAddTorsionFree (Algebra.GrothendieckAddGroup Q ⧸
        AddSubgroup.closure (Algebra.GrothendieckAddGroup.of '' (F : Set Q))) := by
  sorry

end AddSubmonoid
